Summary: D3DMetal: let libd3dshared call ntdll's syscalls with the Microsoft ABI
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover
  Version: 25.1.1
  CW-Hacks: 23015
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz
  Note: CrossOver 25.1.1 CW HACK 23015 (dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h, server.c, sync.c,
    thread.c), without the esync/msync hunks CrossOver has in the same functions
Upstream: no
Why: libd3dshared calls NtClose, NtCreateThreadEx and the event/semaphore syscalls in
 ntdll.so directly with the Microsoft x64 ABI. Each becomes an asm wrapper that jumps to an
 ms_abi thunk when the caller's return address is inside libd3dshared, and to the normal
 (renamed sysv_*) function otherwise. Needs ntdll-d3dmetal-code-regions (libd3dshared_load_addr/_code_end).
 (On 10.0: CrossOver's esync/msync changes edit the bodies of the same
 functions in sync.c and server.c; this patch only renames them and adds
 code after them.)
Programs: none known
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: ntdll.so's exported NtClose, NtCreateSemaphore, NtReleaseSemaphore,
 NtCreateEvent, NtSetEvent, NtResetEvent, NtClearEvent, NtPulseEvent and NtCreateThreadEx
 (and no other Nt* export) start with the wrapper: push %rax; push %rcx; compare the return
 address against two globals; jmp to one of two bodies
Expects before it: ntdll-d3dmetal-code-regions; libd3dshared_load_addr is defined only
 there

